# Pin line endings for tracked text files.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on every
# checkout. Two things broke because of it, both found by running the delivered work:
#
#   1. `governance.py` hashes files byte-for-byte. A merge rewrote the line endings of 50
#      files, so `verify` reported BASELINE_CHANGED for a tree `git status` called clean.
#   2. Vite's SSR transform hoists imports above a shebang. With CRLF its shebang
#      detection fails, leaving `#!/usr/bin/env node` on line 8 of the output — not a
#      shebang any more, just a syntax error. `scripts/ui-contract.mjs` stopped loading
#      under vitest while still running fine under plain `node`.
#
# Normalising in the repository and checking out LF everywhere removes both. Binary
# files are marked so git never touches them.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite binary

# 资料库/：归档的原件，按字节保存。
#
# 这里的东西不是本仓库写的文本：PDF 与网页存档有一部分是经互联网档案馆的原始字节接口
# 取回的，`04_文本层/` 是逐字核对过的抽取结果，报告里标「逐字」的引文要能在其中检索到。
# 让 `* text=auto eol=lf` 去规范化它们的行尾，等于改写归档件本身（CR-20260915-library-adoption CP-1）。
资料库/** -text
